    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0608" n="506" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg506"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 13329/4–5.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador O’Brien to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 309.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the department’s telegram of the 1st instant,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d483-f1"/>
                    and to inclose herewith copy of note which I to-day personally handed to the
                    minister for foreign affairs concerning the matter. Count Hayashi, in the course
                    of the interview which I had with him, begged me to transmit to the department
                    the Japanese Government’s deep appreciation and thanks for the message of
                    sympathy.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. J. O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d483-a1.xml" xpointer="d483-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
